[2] THE CASCADE: do binding runners form a SYMMETRY ORBIT? (reflection x→−x mod n)
    tight/symmetric configs should have their pins replicate through symmetry.
    AP {1..6}        n= 7 speeds±-sym mod n=True  binders=[3, 4]  binders ±-closed mod n=True
    AP {1..13}       n=14 speeds±-sym mod n=True  binders=[5, 9]  binders ±-closed mod n=True
    transl {7..12}   n= 7 speeds±-sym mod n=False  binders=[7, 12]  binders ±-closed mod n=False
    generic A        n= 7 speeds±-sym mod n=False  binders=[3, 5, 11, 17, 29, 41]  binders ±-closed mod n=False

[3] THE APEX as reflection fixed point (even n: runner n/2 sits at frac=1/2)
    n=6: apex=3, frac(apex·t*)=0.5000 (→ reflection fixed pt 1/2), ‖apex·t*‖=0.5000 (max possible) — the safest spot, a non-smooth pin
    n=10: apex=5, frac(apex·t*)=0.5000 (→ reflection fixed pt 1/2), ‖apex·t*‖=0.5000 (max possible) — the safest spot, a non-smooth pin
    n=14: apex=7, frac(apex·t*)=0.5000 (→ reflection fixed pt 1/2), ‖apex·t*‖=0.5000 (max possible) — the safest spot, a non-smooth pin

[4] SUMMARY — the rigidity duality
    TIGHT configs: avg binding=2.0, avg 3term=21.0, all local-rigid=True
    SAFE  configs: avg binding=4.7, avg 3term=1.2
    => symmetry (3-term/AP) ⇒ large binding orbit ⇒ witness-rigid (tight);
       asymmetry ⇒ small generic binding ⇒ witness-flexible (safe).

[5] RIGOR: is 'binding set closed under a symmetry of the speed set' the tight discriminator?
    Test reflection x→a−x and dilation x→cx mod n that fix the speed set, check binders orbit-closed.
    AP {1..6} (tight)          n= 7 G=0.1429 δ=0.1429 TIGHT | #speed-syms=5 binders=[3, 4] closed under [(6, 0)]
    sporadic {1,3,4,7} n=5     n= 5 G=0.2000 δ=0.2000 TIGHT | #speed-syms=3 binders=[2, 3] closed under [(4, 0)]
    sporadic {1,3,4,5,9} n=6   n= 6 G=0.1667 δ=0.1667 TIGHT | #speed-syms=1 binders=[1, 5] closed under NONE
    transl {7..12} (safe)      n= 7 G=0.3684 δ=0.1429 safe  | #speed-syms=5 binders=[0, 5] closed under [(6, 5)]
    generic A (safe)           n= 7 G=0.5000 δ=0.1429 safe  | #speed-syms=1 binders=[1, 3, 4, 5, 6] closed under [(6, 2)]
    => tight configs: binding set is invariant under a nontrivial speed-set symmetry (a cascade orbit);
       safe configs: no nontrivial symmetry, binders generic. Local pin (apex/fixed pt) vs global orbit.
